      "writtenOn": "2019-02-08T16:07:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not clear from the code in this file what the policy should be about preserving order vs. re-sorting frequently. Some places use ImmutableSet, which is order-preserving; some use TreeSet, which sorts; this one uses HashSet which is not order-preserving.\n\nI would be in favor of consistently using (Immutable)SortedSets for all local variables, method arguments, and return values, so it\u0027s easier to reason about.\n\n(There could be an argument for favoring order-preserving over sorted sets, to avoid churn in the case where a human accidentally unsorts the list. But this is not something that should ever be touched by humans, and if they do, they can live with the churn.)",
      "revId": "67c2a5a65f89b6a61681bae56973db2bf44c12f6",
